pr_body:
Fixes: https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/108423

Handles duplicate keys that are encountered when reporting telemetry and using the cat API for trained models. Duplicates can occur because a single model id can have multiple deployments. The current implementation uses the model id for keys in various maps. The model id is used to get access to stats about the model itself and we don't actually need the individual deployments. Because of this, I just take the first occurrence and ignore duplicates.

For some reason the estimated heap bytes needed for elser only shows 0 🤔 I tested on main and it happens there too so I don't believe it's related to this PR.

## Testing

Download elser, start a few deployments, perform inference a few times

```
GET _cat/ml/trained_models?v&h=id,ic,icurr,if,ip,it,o,v

PUT _ingest/pipeline/elser
{
  "processors": [
    {
      "inference": {
        "model_id": "dep1",
        "input_output": [
            {
                "input_field": "column2",
                "output_field": "text_embedding"
            }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "set": {
        "field": "timestamp",
        "value": "{{_ingest.timestamp}}"
      }
    }
  ]
}

PUT _ingest/pipeline/elser
{
  "processors": [
    {
      "inference": {
        "model_id": "dep1",
        "input_output": [
            {
                "input_field": "column2",
                "output_field": "text_embedding"
            }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "set": {
        "field": "timestamp",
        "value": "{{_ingest.timestamp}}"
      }
    }
  ]
}

PUT _ingest/pipeline/elser5
{
  "processors": [
    {
      "inference": {
        "model_id": "dep2",
        "input_output": [
            {
                "input_field": "column2",
                "output_field": "text_embedding"
            }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "set": {
        "field": "timestamp",
        "value": "{{_ingest.timestamp}}"
      }
    }
  ]
}

POST _ingest/pipeline/elser/_simulate
{
  "docs": [
    {
      "_source": {
        "column2": "hello"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

Should return the number of ingest pipelines associated and inference counts

```
id                          ic icurr if ip it  o     v      hs
.elser_model_2_linux-x86_64 3  0     0  5  270 0     12.0.0 0b
lang_ident_model_1          0  0     0  0  0   39629 7.6.0  1mb
```

